From d89e4ea4543854c0138bbb76ac85dad562ebdcc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 07:30:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 132/145] media: meson: vdec: hevc: read references as NV12,
 not NV21

The VP9 codec clears HEVCD_IPP_AXIIF_CONFIG bit 12 when it programs the
IPP AXI interface, and has since VP9 support was added: the hardware's
native chroma order for that read path is NV21, and this driver hands
the engine NV12 planes.  codec_hevc_set_sao() programs the same register
from the same values but never clears the bit, so the motion compensator
reads every reference frame's chroma with Cb and Cr the wrong way round.

Only 8-bit NV12M output is affected.  It is the only mode where the
references the MC reads are the NV12 planes themselves; 10-bit predicts
from the compressed body and comes out with correct colour, which is
what the two cases look like on a gxbb board: 8-bit decodes to blocks of
green and magenta that get worse the further the stream runs from the
last intra frame, 10-bit does not.

Fixes: a2494e69efa4 ("media: meson: vdec: HEVC decode on G12A/G12B (8-bit and 10-bit)")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
index c3b4fb0ba020..c0a189cfaeb6 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -589,8 +589,10 @@ static void codec_hevc_show_frames(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 		    (hevc->frames_num <= tmp->num_reorder_pic))
 			break;
 
-		dev_dbg(sess->core->dev, "DONE frame poc %u; vbuf %u\n",
-			tmp->poc, tmp->vbuf->vb2_buf.index);
+		dev_dbg(sess->core->dev,
+			"DONE frame poc %u; vbuf %u; reorder %u; held %u\n",
+			tmp->poc, tmp->vbuf->vb2_buf.index,
+			tmp->num_reorder_pic, hevc->frames_num);
 		amvdec_dst_buf_done_offset(sess, tmp->vbuf, tmp->offset,
 					   V4L2_FIELD_NONE, 0, false);
 
@@ -1258,6 +1260,7 @@ codec_hevc_set_sao(struct amvdec_session *sess, struct hevc_frame *frame)
 
 	val = amvdec_read_dos(core, HEVCD_IPP_AXIIF_CONFIG) & ~0x30;
 	val |= 0xf;
+	val &= ~BIT(12); /* NV12 */
 	amvdec_write_dos(core, HEVCD_IPP_AXIIF_CONFIG, val);
 
 	val = 0;
-- 
